  partName: Spark Plug (5)
  description: The Spark Plug (5) is a tiny, elongated component situated at the
    top-right-rear of the engine, constructed from Material.001, responsible for
    generating the high-voltage spark that ignites the fuel-air mixture. Its tiny
    size belies its importance, as it enables the engine to run efficiently, and
    a notable aspect is that it is designed to withstand the harsh conditions inside
    the combustion chamber. The spark plug's location at the top-right-rear allows
    for optimal spark delivery to the fuel-air mixture.
